# 🚀 Namma Ride App: Fast Build Checklist

## 1. Finalize MVP Features
- [ ] List core features (User Auth, Ride Booking, Payment, AI suggestions)
- [ ] Define user stories for each feature

## 2. Project Structure
- [ ] Organize folders for frontend, backend, assets, docs
- [ ] Ensure README.md and CONTRIBUTING.md are updated

## 3. Development Setup
- [ ] Set up Flutter/React Native environment
- [ ] Initialize backend (Node.js, Django, etc. as needed)
- [ ] Set up database (Firebase, MongoDB, etc.)

## 4. Automate Workflow
- [ ] Add GitHub Actions for CI/CD
- [ ] Add linters and formatters for code quality

## 5. Build Core Features
- [ ] Implement User Registration/Login
- [ ] Implement Ride Booking logic
- [ ] Integrate Payment Gateway
- [ ] Develop AI-powered ride suggestions

## 6. Testing
- [ ] Write unit and integration tests
- [ ] Automate tests with GitHub Actions

## 7. Early Deployment & Feedback
- [ ] Deploy to test/staging environment
- [ ] Share early build for feedback

## 8. Documentation
- [ ] Update README with setup, usage, and API docs
- [ ] Add code comments and examples

## 9. Community & Contribution
- [ ] Create issues for remaining tasks
- [ ] Label issues (good first issue, help wanted)
- [ ] Engage contributors and merge PRs quickly

## 10. Iterate for Release
- [ ] Collect feedback and fix bugs
- [ ] Polish UI/UX
- [ ] Prepare for production launch

